    "ls|LS16_S14_U_534": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*534 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04-04-2018 \n \n \nAADHAAR  LINKAGE \n \n*534.     SHRI KAPIL MORESHWAR PATIL: \n \nWill the Minister of ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)   whether the Government is aware of the grave inconvenience and difficulties being faced \nby the senior citizens in getting their Aadhaar linked to various services on account of \nbiometric machines failing to read their fading finger prints and the service p roviders \nadvising them to get their finger prints re-verified again and again;  \n \n(a) if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken by the Government to help and \nfacilitate the senior citizens to end their plight; and  \n \n(c)    the outcome thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A statement  is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED  \nQUESTION NO.*534 FOR 04.04.2018 REGARDING AADHAAR LINKAGE \n………. \n  \n(a), (b) and (c): Aadhaar Authentication using fingerprint depends upon number of factors viz. \nquality of fingerprint, network connectivity, placement of finger etc.  However, few senior \ncitizens, persons engaged in manual labour or individuals with specific disabilities m ay face \ndifficulties in fingerprint authentication. \n \nUIDAI provides various modes of authentication viz Demographic, Biometric (Finger Print + \nIRIS), OTP and Multi-factor authentication. The Service Provider may choose suitable mode(s) of \nauthentication. \n \nAs per para 14(1)(i) of Aadhaar (Authentication) Regulation 2016, a requesting entity has to \nimplement exception -handing mechanisms and back -up identity authentication mechanisms to \nensure seamless provision of authentication services to Aadhaar number holders. \n \nFurther, DBT Mission, Cabinet Secretariat vide their letter dated 19.12.2017 has issued guidelines \non exception handling for use of Aadhaar in benefit schemes of Government, which inter -alia has \nstipulated the following mechanism in respect of cases where Aadhaar authentication fails: \n \ni.  Departments and Bank Branches may make provisions for IRIS scanners along with \nfingerprint scanners, wherever feasible. \n \nii.   In cases of failure due to lack of connectivity, offline authentication system such as QR \ncode bases coupons, Mobile based OTP or TOTP may be explored. \n \niii.   In all cases where online authentication is not feasible, the benefit/ service may be \nprovided on the basis of possession of Aadhaar, after duly recording the transaction in \nregister, to be reviewed and audited periodically. \n \n****** \n\n  \n\n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_535": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 535 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MEGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nUTILISATION CERTIFICATES FOR MPF FUNDS \n \n535. SHRI KONDA VISHWESHWAR REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether all the State Governments have submitted Utilisation \nCertificates for the funds released for 2015 and 2016 under the \nModernisation of Police Force (MPF) Scheme as per General Financial Rules \nwhich is required for release of further funds and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether concurrent audit of MPF Scheme by the Internal Audit Wing of \nthe Ministry of Home Affairs has been conducted to curb corruption/misuse \nof funds for the past three years; and \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n(a) No, Madam. Under the scheme of Modernisation of Police Forces(MPF), \nUtilisation Certificates(UCs) for the funds released up to the financial year \n2015-16, which are required for release of further funds as per General \nFinancial Rules, are awaited from the following States, as on 05.02.2018, for \nthe amount shown against them:  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n     \n\n                      \n-2- \nLS.US.Q.No.535 FOR 06.02.2018 \n \n              (in Rs. Crore) \nS. \nNo. \nName of the \nState \nPending \namount in \nrespect of \nwhich UC \nis pending \nS. \nNo. \nName of the \nState \nPending \namount in \nrespect of \nwhich UC \nis pending \n1. Arunachal \nPradesh \n3.12 13. Maharashtra 86.74 \n2. Assam 91.13 14. Manipur 5.50 \n3. Bihar 26.32 15. Meghalaya 1.35 \n4. Chhattisgarh 8.65 16. Orissa 0.29 \n5. Goa 1.36 17. Punjab 4.94 \n6. Haryana 1.37 18. Rajasthan 0.02 \n7. Himachal \nPradesh \n0.44 19. Tamil Nadu 32.93 \n8. Jammu & \nKashmir \n3.55 20. Tripura 13.71 \n9. Jharkhand 10.56 21. Uttar Pradesh 53.84 \n10. Karnataka 6.70 22. Uttarakhand 1.49 \n11. Kerala 4.70 23. West Bengal 75.77 \n12. Madhya Pradesh 4.57  Total 439.04 \n \n(b) & (c)  Audit of MPF Scheme for the period up to 31.3.2016 has been \nconducted for all the States by the Internal Audit Wing of the Ministry of \nHome Affairs.  The Audit for the year 2016 -17 has been conducted of all the \nStates except Kerala, Bihar, Telangana and Goa.  \n \n***** \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_536": "PRIORITY-XVI\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.536         \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2018\nINDIAN WORKERS RESOURCE CENTRE\n *536.  SHRI ANTO ANTONY:\nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has any scheme to set up Indian Workers\nResource Centre (IWRC) and if so, the details including the salient\nfeatures thereof;\n(b) the  details  of  IWRCs  already  established  in  various  countries,\ncountry-wise along with the major services offered by IWRCs; \n(c) whether the Government has received any proposal for setting up\nsome more IWRCs;\n(d) if  so,  the  details  thereof  and  the  response  of  the  Government\nthereto; and  \n(e) whether the Government proposes to set up some more IWRCs and\nif so, the details thereof? \nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER FOR EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRIMATI SUSHMA SWARAJ)\n (a) to (e) A statement is laid on the T able of the House.\n*****\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF THE LOK\nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 536 REGARDING “INDIAN WORKERS\nRESOURCE CENTRE” FOR ANSWER ON 04.04.2018\n(a) & (b) Yes Madam. Indian Worker Resource Centres (IWRCs) have already\nbeen setup in Dubai and Sharjah (UAE), Riyadh and Jeddah (Saudi Arabia) and Kuala\nLumpur to provide guidance and counselling on all matters pertaining to overseas\nIndian workers. \nFollowing are some of the major activities of IWRCs:\n(i) 24x7 HELP LINES in all 5 centres which have been receiving, registering and\nmonitoring grievance petitions of Indians and providing necessary advice /\nresolution and providing clarification to information seeking queries.  If not\nresolved,  the  cases  are  escalated  to  the  Embassy  /Consulate  for  further\nresolution.\n(ii) Providing counseling sessions on legal, financial, medical and psychological\nmatters.\n(iii) Awareness camps that are conducted in labour camps which   educates the\nworkers on various issues they face during their employment, health related\ntalks by experts, various schemes of Govt of India for the welfare of the\nworkers.\n(iv) Liaising with help-groups, individuals, social workers and related bodies to\noffer assistance to Indian Community Members.\n(v) To verify the genuineness of job offers received by Indians from companies in\nthe respective countries.\n(c) to (e) The Government is in favour of setting up of IWRCs in the Missions in\nECR countries in case such a need is felt by our Missions, based on local situation.\nAs and when proposals are received for setting up of more IWRCs, the same are\nconsidered expeditiously on merits.  A recent proposal from Indian Mission in Qatar\nfor setting up of an IWRC has been accorded in-principle approval.\n*****",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_537": "PRIOTIRY-XVII\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n \nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO.537\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2018\n \nAUSTRALIA GROUP\n \n*537. SHRI CH. MALLA REDDY:\n Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n \n(a)  whether  India  has  been  admitted  as  the  43rd member  of  the\nAustralia Group;\n(b)  if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) the benefits accrued by joining the Group including keeping a tight\ncontrol over exports of substances used in the making of chemical\nweapons? \nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER FOR EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n(SHRIMATI SUSHMA SWARAJ)\n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the T able of the House. \n*****\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF THE LOK\nSABHA  STARRED  QUESTION  NO.  537  REGARDING  “AUSTRALIA\nGROUP” FOR ANSWER ON 04.04.2018\n India  joined  the  Australia  Group  on  19  January  2018  following  the\ncompletion of internal procedures for joining the Group. The Australia Group decided\nto admit India as the Group’s 43rd Participant through a consensus decision.\nIndia’s chemical and biotechnology sectors are significant contributors in the\nGDP. Membership of the Australia Group (AG) will ease the access to chem-bio\ntechnologies and enable our competitive and growing chemical and biotechnology\nsectors to increase their share in international trade of value added chem-bio items. \nProliferation of dual-use chemicals is a cause for concern given the increasing\naccess to such items by terrorists and non-state actors and their illicit use in chemical\nweapons. India’s membership of the AG would be mutually beneficial and further\ncontribute to international security and non-proliferation objectives. India’s export\ncontrol regulations will not impede the normal trade of materials and equipment used\nfor legitimate purposes.\n*****",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_538": "    GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.538 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.04.2018 \n \nPRIMARY HEALTH SERVICES AND DIAGNOSTIC CENTRES \n \n*538.  SHRI ANIL SHIROLE:  \n           SHRI PARBHUBHAI NAGARBHAI VASAVA: \n \n       Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways is planning to open Primary Health Care and \nBasic Diagnostic Centres at many of the railway stations across the \ncountry including Maharashtra, Gujarat and West Bengal; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise and the reasons therefor; \n(c) the details of the funds likely to be sanctioned for this purpose and \nthe time by which these centres are likely to be opened; \n(d) whether the Railways has tied up with the Ministry of  Health and \nFamily Welfare in this regard and if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) whether the Railways has opened such centres at any of the railway \nstations in the country and if so, the details thereof along with the \nresponse received thereto? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COAL \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n***** \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO REPLY IN PARTS (a) TO (e) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO.538 BY SHRI ANIL SHIROLE AND SHRI PARBHUBHAI \nNAGARBHAI VASAVA TO BE  ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 04.04.2018 \nREGARDING PRIMARY HEALTH SERVICES AND DIAGNOSTIC CENTRES \n \n(a): No, Madam. However, in compliance of orders of Hon’ble Supreme \nCourt and as recommended by Committee of experts constituted at All \nIndia Institute of Medica l Sciences (AIIMS) , instructions have been \nissued to provide a Medical Box containing life saving medicines, \nequipments, oxygen cylinder etc. at all R ailway stations. Front line staff \ni.e. Train Ticket Examiner, Train Superintendents, Assistant Station \nMaster etc. are trained in rendering First Aid. Regular refresher courses \nare conducted for such staff. List of near -by hospitals and doctors along \nwith their contact numbers is available at all Railway Stations. \nAmbulance services of Railways, State Governme nt/ Private Hospitals \nand ambulance service providers are utilized to transport the injured/ \nsick passengers to the hospitals/ doctor’s clinics. In Mumbai \n(Maharashtra) sub-urban stations, specific space has been allocated for \nparking of State Government A mbulance and at 24 stations , Emergency \nMedical Rooms with private doctors have been established.  \n \n(b) to (e): Do not arise. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_539": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 539 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MEGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nRAISING ADDITIONAL BATTALIONS FOR BORDER SECURITY \n \n539. SHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether his Ministry has any proposal for creation of a 29 -battalion Indo \nMyanmar Border Force to patrol India’s 1643 long mountainous border with \nMyanmar;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the aims and objective behind the move;  \n \n(c) the composition of the proposed battalion;  \n \n(d) the expenditure likely to be incurred for raising this battalion;  \n \n(e) whether the Government is considering to deploy the en tire ITBP on the \nMyanmar border; and \n \n(f) if so, the details thereof along with the time by which this new battalion is \nlikely to be created and put into operation? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) to (f): Based on security requirement s and availability of resources, \nstrengthening and streamlining of border guarding arrangements is an \nongoing and continuous process. However, as of now, no decision has been \ntaken on the creation of Indo-Myanmar Border Force. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_540": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.540 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2018 \n \nRASHTRIYA  GOKUL  MISSION \n \n540. SHRI  LAXMI NARAYAN YADAV: \n \n    Will the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE �� �� ���� ���������������������������������������� \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Sagar region of Madhya Pradesh has been covered under the Rashtriya Gokul Mission; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n  \n(c) the details of the works carried out by the Government so far in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE  FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \n(SHRIMATI  KRISHNA  RAJ) \n \n \n(a)to(c): Yes, Sir. The Rashtriya Gokul  Mission is not region specific; all the Districts of the \nState are covered under the scheme. The proposal submitted by the State under Rashtriya Gokul \nMission (RGM) has been approved with an allocation of Rs .104.69 crore and out of this an amount \nof Rs.68.51 crores has been released to the State for implementation of the project. Details of the \nworks carried out by the State under the scheme is at Annexure-I. \n \n \n \n******  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO THE PART (a) TO (c) OF THE LOK SABHA \nQUESTION NO. 540 DUE FOR ANSWER ON 06.02.2018 \nANNEXURE-I \n \nWORKS/ACTIVITIES UNDERTAKEN BY THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH \nUNDER  RASHTRIYA GOKUL MISSION \nS. No. Components  Achievements \nupto Dec 2017 \n1 Extension of field AI network    \n1.1 Training of new MAITRI's (in number) 1296 \n1.2 Refresher training  to MAITRI's (in Nos) 123 \n1.3 Equipments (Cryo Cans, AI kit, Trevis, Castrator) (number of set) 1296 \n1.5 Tappering Grants (to number of MAITRIs) 1296 \n1.6 Training of existing AI worker (to number of technicians) 895 \n2 Strengthening of existing AI centres   \n2.1 Replacement of cryo containers (number of AI centres) 3536 \n2.2 Replacement of AI kits (number of AI centres) 1887 \n3 Monitoring of AI programme    \n3.1 Identification of females covered through AI (No. of tags purchased) 450000 \n3.2 Tagging Applicators (Nos of applicators) 3400 \n4 Development & Conservation of Indigenous Breeds   \n4.1 Award to Best Breeders Society 1 \n5 Manpower development    \n5.1 Establishment & Strengthening of training centres (number) 6 \n5.2 Establishment of regional/farmers training centres (number) 1 \n5.3 Trainers Training Program (number of trainers) 4 \n5.4 Farmer Orientation Program (number of farmers) 40000 \n5.5 Training of Professionals (number) 178 \n5.6 Organization of seminars & workshops (District level, State Level and \nNational level) number 4 \n6 Strengthening LN Transport and Distribution system   \n6.1 Bulk LN Transport storage & Distribution system upto AI centres \n(number) 3 \n7 Procurement of Bulls for NS & AI   \n7.1 Procurement of Male calves for NS (number o[f bulls) 600 \n7.2 Feeding of Male calves 600 \n7.3 Procurement of Bulls for AI (number of bulls) 181 \n8 Control of infertility & reduction of intercalving period   \n8.1 Organization of Fertility camps (number) 200 \n8.2 Oestrus Synchronization (number of animals) 50 \n8.3 Organization of Calf Rallies (number of rallies) 2 \n8.4 Publicity & Extension Materials (number of pamphlets printed 174000 \n \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_541": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE,\n \nCOOPERATION\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n541\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \nTHE \n6\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, \n2018\n \n \nPROMOTION OF AGRO\n-\nFORESTRY AND ORCHARDS\n \n \n541.\n \n \nSHRI\n \nBHEEMRAO B. PATIL:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n  \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nwhether the Government proposes to promote agro\n-\nforestry and orchards in various \nStates of the country including tribal and backward areas of Andhra Pradesh and Telangana; \n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the details th\nereof; and \n \n \n(c) \n \nthe details of the financial assistance provided to various States for the said purpose \nduring the last three years and the current year, State/UT\n-\nwise?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nए\nवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी\n \n \n   \n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT)\n \n \n(a)\n \n&\n \n(b)\n:\n \n \nYes\n,\n \nMadam.\n \n \n(i) \n \nFor promotion of agro\n-\nforestry in the country, Government of India has launched \nSub\n-\nMission on Agroforestry (SMAF) from the year 2016\n-\n17. The schem\ne is to be \nimplemented in those States /UTs which have liberalized transit regulations for transport \nof timber.  The scheme is being implemented in Andhra Pradesh since 2016\n-\n17. \nTelangana has recently liberalized transit regulations for transport of timber\n \nbut the \nannual action plan for the scheme has not been received as yet. \n \n \n(ii)\n \n \nMission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH), a Centrally \nSponsored Scheme is being implemented from the year 2014\n-\n15 for holistic growth of \nthe horticulture sect\nor including orchards. The Mission envisages enhancing production \nand productivity of fruits and vegetables through various interventions and is being \nimplemented in Andhra Pradesh and Telangana also.\n \n \n \n(c):\n \nState /UT wise details for Sub\n-\nMission on Agrofo\nrestry and Mission for Integrated \nDevelopment of Horticulture are placed at Annexure\n-\nI &II, respectively.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \nANNEXURE\n-\nI\n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART \n(c)\n \nOF THE LOK SABHA\n \nUN\nSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. \n541\n \nREGARDING ‘\nPROMOTION OF AGRO\n-\nFORESTRY AN\nD ORCHARDS\n” \nDUE FOR REPLY ON 06\n.\n02\n.2018\n \n \nStatement \nof \nfinancial assistance provided by the Government to\n \nStates\n \nunder Sub\n-\nMission on Agrofo\nr\nestry (SMAF)\n*\n \n \nName of State\n \nAmount Released (\nRs. in lakhs)\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n2017\n-\n18\n \n(as on 01.02.2018)\n \nAn\ndhra\n \nPradesh\n \n315\n.00\n \n0.00\n \nBihar\n \n0.00\n \n300.00\n \nChhatishgarh\n \n0.00\n \n250.00\n \nGujarat\n \n450.00\n \n0.00\n \nHaryana\n \n175.00\n \n0.00\n \nHim\nachal\n \nPradesh\n \n115.00\n \n48.69\n \nJharkhand\n \n0.00\n \n400.00\n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \n0.00\n \n60.71\n \nKarnataka\n \n325.00\n \n450.00\n \nKerala\n \n0.00\n \n206.47\n \nMadhya \nPradesh\n \n420.00\n \n0.00\n \nMaha\nrashtra\n \n0.00\n \n400.00\n \nMeghalaya\n \n0.00\n \n100.00\n \nO\ndisha\n \n0.00\n \n400.00\n \nPunjab\n \n200.00\n \n0.00\n \nRajasthan\n \n0.00\n \n600.00\n \nTamil Nadu\n \n250.00\n \n0.00\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n0.00\n \n600.00\n \nTOTAL \n \n2250\n.00\n \n3815.87\n \n       \n \n      \n* The scheme was launched in\n \n2016\n-\n17\n \n\n \nANNEXURE\n-\nI\nI\n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART \n(c)\n \nOF THE LOK SABHA\n \nUN\nSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. \n541\n \nREGARDING ‘\nPROMOTION OF AGRO\n-\nFORESTRY AND ORCHARDS\n” \nDUE FOR REPLY ON 06\n.\n02\n.2018\n \n \nStatement indicating \nfinancial assistance provided by the Governm\nent to States/ UTs\n \nunder \nMission for Int