    "ls|LS16_S14_U_588": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 588 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MEGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF BUNKERS AT LoC \n \n588. SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has  recently taken a decision to construct  \ncommunity and individual bunkers from the  point of security at the Indo -Pak \nborder; \n \n(b) if so, whether the Government has  prepared a blueprint and fixed a time -\nlimit in this regard; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof along with  the number of bunkers constructed at \nthe Indo-Pak border at present; \n \n(d) whether the Government proposes  to give shelters to the local people in \nthese bunkers from the security point of view; and \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (e): Yes, Madam. In order to mitigate the hardships being faced by \npeople living on the International Border/LoC due to Cross Border Firing, the \nMinistry of Home Affairs has recently approved a proposal for construction of \n14460 bunkers. These include 1431 large Community Bunkers and 13029 \nIndividual Bunkers in the Districts of Samba, Jammu, Kathua, Poonch and \nRajouri. The project is being implemented by the State Government of \nJammu & Kashmir. \n***** \n                                                           ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_589": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY, DAIRYING AND FISHERIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.589 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2018 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF FISHERIES \n \n 589.    SHRI NALIN KUMAR KATEEL:  \n SHRI D.K. SURESH:  \n SHRI B.N. CHANDRAPPA:                   \n \n      Will the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE क ृ षि और ककसान कल्याण मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether it is a fact that Fisheries is an important economic activity and a flour ishing sector \nwith varied resources and potential in the country and if so, the details of the growth witnessed \nduring the recent years; \n \n(b) whether the Government has maintained any data about the number of people engaged for \nlivelihood in the fisheries sector in the country and if so the details thereof, State-wise;  \n \n(c) whether the Government is taking various steps to attract more number of people to the sector \nby promoting and allocation of adequate funds for the fisheries sector;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(e) whether it is also a fact that there is immense scope for the further development of the \nfisheries and aquaculture sector in the country; and  \n \n(f) if so, the measures taken by the Government  during the last three years and the details \nthereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \n(SHRIMATI  KRISHNA RAJ) \n \n(a): Yes, Madam. Fisheries is an important economic activity and a flourishing sector with \nvaried resources and potential in the country. The details of the growth rate in fish production \nwitnessed during the last three years in inland and marine sector is given below: \nFinancial \nYear \nInland Marine Total \nProduction \n(lakh \ntonnes)  \nGrowth \nRate (%) \nProduction \n(lakh \ntonnes)  \nGrowth \nRate (%) \nProduction \n(lakh tonnes)  \nGrowth \nRate \n(%) \n2014-15 66.91 9.04 35.69 3.66 102.60 7.1 \n2015-16 71.62 7.04 36.00 0.87 107.62 4.9 \n2016-17 (P) 77.68 8.46 36.41 1.14 114.09 6.0 \n\n \n(b):  Yes, Madam. The Department has maintained data of the number of fishers engaged for \nlivelihood in the fisheries sector in the country. The statement showing State -wise details of \nnumber of fishers engaged in fisheries sector are furnished at Annexure A. \n \n(c)&(d): Yes, Madam. The Department is taking various steps to attract more number of people \nto the fisheries sector by implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme (CSS) ‘Blue Revolution: \nIntegrated Development and Management of Fisheries’ and allocation of adequate funds to \nvarious States/UTs. A statement showing the State-wise details of tentative funds allocated under \nthe CSS during the current financial year (2017-18) is at Annexure B. \n \n(e)&(f): Yes, Madam. There is immense scope for the further development of the fisheries a nd \naquaculture sector in the country. The Department has provided financial assistance to various \nStates/UTs for development of Inland fisheries and Aquaculture, Marine fisheries and post \nharvest infrastructure, welfare of fishermen, Strengthening of Datab ase & Geographical \nInformation System of the Fisheries Sector and Monitoring, Control and Surveillance (MCS) and \nother need -based Interventions. The details of funds released by the Department for the \ndevelopment of fisheries sector to various States and UTs during last three years are as under: \n \n \n \n \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nFinancial Year Amount Released (Rs in lakh) \n2014-15 35335.98 \n2015-16 41680.94 \n2016-17 42411.00 \n\nANNEXURE- A  \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.589 TO BE ANSWERED ON 6TH FEBRUARY, 2018 \n \nSTATE-WISE DETAILS OF NUMBER OF FISHERS ENGAGED IN FISHERIES \n \n             Total Number of members \nS.No. State Name Male  Female  Children Total \n1 Andhra Pradesh 249386 250877 393102 893365 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 1650 1376 1373 4399 \n3 Assam 131312 97986 161082 390380 \n4 Bihar 1391166 1266997 2301353 4959516 \n5 Chhatisgarh 621607 529697 760064 1911368 \n6 Goa 5521 4863 3586 13970 \n7 Gujarat 134475 129900 228880 493255 \n8 Haryana 5910 3322 7259 16491 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 1537 1372 2713 5622 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 9628 7593 13232 30453 \n11 Jharkhand 577908 571584 781428 1930920 \n12 Karnataka 55809 52898 50245 158952 \n13 Kerala 224007 317758 206072 747837 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 213888 200607 302479 716974 \n15 Maharashtra 63354 46603 61873 171830 \n16 Manipur 25009 24091 21368 70468 \n17 Meghalaya 525 504 1354 2383 \n18 Mizoram 5498 5312 7097 17907 \n19 Nagaland 5762 5519 3581 14862 \n20 Odisha 70971 48334 60721 180026 \n21 Punjab 2150 1874 5061 9085 \n22 Rajasthan 2638 1693 2985 7316 \n23 Sikkim 9893 8353 8568 26814 \n24 Tamilnadu 171992 156107 148519 476618 \n25 Tripura 15966 13177 17590 46733 \n26 Uttar Pradesh 70373 48892 59799 179064 \n27 Uttaranchal 32 23 35 90 \n28 West Bengal 587214 205198 119210 911622 \n29 Andaman & Nicobar 9859 7693 0 17552 \n30 Chandigarh 198 109 172 479 \n31 Dadra & Nagar Haveli 0 0 0 0 \n32 Daman & Diu 7649 7756 10080 25485 \n33 Delhi 485 475 1555 2515 \n34 Lakshadweep 10408 2621 0 13029 \n35 Puducherry 12378 12799 12797 37974 \n  Total 4696158 4033963 5755233 14485354 \n \n \nSource: 17th Live Stock Census 2003 (Appeared in \nthe Handbook on Fisheries Statistics 2014) \n \n        \n               \n\n  ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_590": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 590 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MEGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nRIOTS AND COMMUNAL VIOLENCE \n \n590. SHRI G. HARI: \n SHRI VENKATESH BABU T.G.: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether incidents of riots/communal violence are on the rise in the  \ncountry and if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(b) the total number of riots/communal violence reported, persons  \nkilled/injured, damages to property, guilty  arrested and the action taken \nagainst them  separately during each of the last three  years and the \ncurrent year, State-wise including Maharashtra; \n \n(c) whether the Government has  assisted the States to control the \nviolence and in itiate action against the  organizations/individuals who \nindulged in such violence and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Government has  directed the police departments to take \nthe strongest action in case of riots/communal  violence and desecratio n \nof religious places and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) the other corrective steps taken  by the Government to check the \nrecurrence of such cases in future? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (c )   As per the available information, the State -wise details of \ncommunal incidents, persons killed/injured therein during 2015, 2016 and \n2017 is enclosed at Annexure-I.   \n“Public Order” and “Police” are State subjects as per the provisions of the \nConstitution of India.  The responsibilities of maintaining law and order, \nincluding investigation, registration/prosecution of crimes, conviction of \naccused,  protection of  life and property etc. and  maintaining relevant \ndata rest  \n\n  \n\n \n \n-2- \nLS.USQ.No.590 FOR 06.02.2018 \nprimarily with the respective State Governments.  The details regarding \npersons arrested/convicted, action taken against them, organizations \ninvolved, damages to property etc. are not maintained centrally. \n(d)  to (e) In order to maintain communal harmony in the co untry, the \nCentral Government assists the State Governments/Union Territory \nAdministrations in a variety of ways like sharing of intelligence, sending \nalert messages, advisories etc. from time to time on important \ndevelopments having bearing on communal ha rmony.  The Central \nGovernment on the requests of the States/Union Territories, sends Central \nArmed Police Forces, including the composite Rapid Action Force, created \nspecially to deal with communal situation. \n \n  The Central Government has issued the Commu nal Harmony \nGuidelines in 2008, which inter -alia lay down standard operating \nprocedures to be put in place to deal with the situations arising out of \ncommunal violence. These guidelines are aimed to maintain due vigilance, \ncareful planning and preparatory measures which may prevent and pre -\nempt many possible incidents of communal violence.  These guidelines \nare reiterated while sending advisories from time to time, particularly \nprior to various religious festivals, with the objective of immediate \nsensitization.    \n***** \n  \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (A) TO (C) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 590 \nFOR  06.02.2018 SHOWING NUMBER OF COMMUNAL INCIDENTS, NUMBER OF PERSONS KILLED/INJURED \nDURING THE YEARS 2015, 2016 and 2017   \n \n \n \n \nState \n2015 2016 2017 \nIncidents \nPersons \nKilled \nPersons \nInjured \nIncidents \nPersons \nKilled \nPersons \nInjured \nIncidents \nPersons \nKilled \nPersons \nInjured \nA & N Islands 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nAndhra Pradesh 4 0 3 1 0 15 1 0 0 \nArunachal Pradesh 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nAssam 3 0 10 12 3 19 16 4 45 \nBihar 71 20 282 65 4 230 85 3 321 \nChandigarh 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 \nChhattisgarh 2 0 10 2 0 6 0 0 0 \nDelhi 5 0 16 7 0 29 3 1 7 \nD & N Haveli 0 0 0 0 0 