    "ls|LS16_S14_U_641": "O.I.H.\n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n641\n                     \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE  \n6\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n, 201\n8\n \n \n       \nNATIONAL \nHORTICULTURE\n \nMISSION\n \n \n641. \n \nSHRIMATI BHAVANA\n \nPUNDALIKRAO\n \nGAWALI PATIL:\n \nSHRI ARVIND SAWANT:\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n  \n‡ãðŠãäÓã \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããè\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n \n(a) \n \nthe number of districts covered\n \nunder the \nNational Horticulture Mission\n \nin the \ncountry along with the State\n-\nwise\n \ndetails thereof;\n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the Government proposes\n \nto expand the National Horticulture\n \nMission in \nthe remaining districts also;\n \n \n(c) \n \nif so, the details thereof, State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n(d) \n \nw\nhether the Government has\n \nreceived representations from various States\n \nto \n \ninclude more number of districts under\n \nthe said Mission; and\n \n \n(e) \n \nif so, the action taken by the\n \nGovernment in this regard?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF  STATE\n \nIN THE  MINISTRY OF  AGRICULTURE AND  FARMERS  WELFARE\n \n \n‡ãðŠãäÓã  \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \n½ãâ¨ããÊã¾ã ½ãñâ Àã•¾ã ½ãâ¨ããè          \n \n( SHRI \nGAJENDRA \nSINGH SHEKHAWAT\n)  \n \n \n(a):\n \nState\n-\nwise details of the total number of districts included under the Mission for \nIntegrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) are at \nAnnexure.\n \n \n(b) & (c):\n \nCurrently there is no such proposal.\n \n \n \n \n\nContd…2/\n-\n \n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \n \n(d) & (e):\n \nYes, Madam. Several requests h\nave been received from various States for \ninclusion of more districts under the Mission. On the issue of inclusion of more districts \nunder MIDH, the view of the department is that while finalizing/indentifying\n \ndistricts for \ninclusion under \nM\nI\nDH, a cluster \napproach for develop\ning \npotential horticultural crops for \nensuring backward and forwarded linkages was adopted. \nThe selection of the district \nwas decided on the comparative advantage of crops based on agro climatic conditions \nand potential for developing m\narketing opportunities. No new districts are being added \nas this may result in thinning out of already limited resources.\n \n \nHowever, there is a provision under MIDH scheme for setting up of infrastructure \nunits relating to post harvest management, marketing\n \nand other projects based activities \nin non\n-\nMIDH districts, provided there is a clear linkage of the units with the horticulture \nproduce. A\npart from this, activities for development of horticulture in non\n-\nMIDH districts \ncan be carried out under other Gover\nnment schemes like Rashtriya Krishi Vikas Yojana \n(RKVY), Mahatama Gandhi \n \nNational Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), \nPramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana (PKVY) etc.\n            \n \n \n \n                    \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nStatement \nshowing State wise Districts covered under MIDH\n \n \nSl. No.\n \nName of States/UTs\n \nNo. of Districts*\n \n1\n \nAndaman & Nicobar\n \nTwo (2)\n \n2\n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \nEleven (11)\n \n3\n \nBihar\n \nTwenty Three (23)\n \n4\n \nChhattisgarh\n \nNineteen (19)\n \n5\n \nDadra & Nagar Haveli\n \nOne (1)\n \n6\n \nDelhi\n \nOne \n(1)\n \n7\n \nGoa\n \nTwo (2)\n \n8\n \nGujarat\n \nFifteen (15)\n \n9\n \nHaryana\n \nEighteen (18)\n \n10\n \nJharkhand\n \nSeventeen (17)\n \n11\n \nKarnataka\n \nThirty (30)\n \n12\n \nKerala\n \nFourteen (14)\n \n13\n \nLakshadweep\n \nOne (1)\n \n14\n \nMaharashtra\n \nThirty Three (33)\n \n15\n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \nThirty Nine (39)\n \n16\n \nOdisha\n \nTwenty Four (24)\n \n17\n \nPunjab\n \nEighteen (18)\n \n18\n \nPuducherry\n \nFour (4)\n \n19\n \nRajasthan\n \nTwenty Four (24)\n \n20\n \nTamil Nadu\n \nTwenty (20)\n \n21\n \nTelangana\n \nNine (9)\n \n22\n \nUttar Pradesh\n \nForty Five (45)\n \n23\n \nWest Bengal\n \nFourteen (14)\n \n24\n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \nTwenty One (21)\n \n25\n \nAssam\n \nThirty Three (33)\n \n26\n \nManipur\n \nSixteen (16)\n \n27\n \nMeghalaya\n \nEleven (11)\n \n28\n \nMizoram\n \nEight (8)\n \n29\n \nNagaland\n \nEleven (11)\n \n30\n \nSikkim\n \nFour (4)\n \n31\n \nTripura\n \nFour\n  \n \n(4)\n \n32\n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \nTwelve (12)\n \n33\n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \nTwenty Two (22)\n \n34\n \n \nUttarakhand\n \nThirteen (13)\n \nTotal\n \n \nFive Hundred Thirty Nine \n(539)\n \n* \nSubsequent to identification of districts for MIDH implementation, some of the MIDH \ndistricts were bifurcated/ merged.\n \n \n\n \n*******\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_642": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 642  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2018 \n \nWELFARE OF TRANSGENDERS  \n \n642. SHRI E.T. MOHAMMED BASHEER:  \n \nWill the Minister of SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the transgender community is deprived of employment, education and status in the \nsociety;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the action proposed to be taken by the Government to ensure social justice to transgender \ncommunities? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR SOCIAL JUSTICE AND EMPOWERMENT \n(SHRI VIJAY SAMPLA) \n(a) to (c): An Expert Committee was constituted in the Ministry to make an in -depth study of the \nproblems being faced by the Tansgender Community and suggest suitable measures to \nameliorate their conditions. The Committe submitted its report on 27 th January 2014. The \nCommittee in its report has observed that the transgender community is a highly marginalized \nand vulnerable one and is seriously lagging behind on human development indices mainly in the \narea of education and employment.  \n In order to provide f or protection of rights of transgender persons and their welfare, the \nMinistry has introduced a Bill titled “The Transgender Persons (Protection of Rights) Bill, 2016” \nin the Lok Sabha on 2.8.2016. The Bill provides for inclusive education for Transgender Persons \nwithout discrimination on an equal basis with others and prohibits the establishments for \ndiscrimination against them in any matter relating to employment. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S14_U_643": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS   \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 643 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 06TH FEBRUARY, 2018/ MAGHA 17, 1939 (SAKA) \n \nFAKE CURRENCY NOTES  \n \n643.   SHRI RAYAPATI SAMBASIVA RAO: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the quantum of fake Indian Currency Notes seized since \ndemonetisation, State/ UT-wise;  \n \n(b) the details of new method that have been put in place since \ndemonetisation to ensure that fake notes are not generated and circulated; \nand  \n \n(c) the details of evidence which has come to light so far with regard to the \nrole of Pakistan in manufacturing fake notes? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n(a) & (b): As per the data available with National Crime Record Bureau  \n(NCRB),  Fake Indian Currency Notes (FICN) of face value of Rs. 21.54 \ncrores  have been seized by State/UTs Police from 09.11.2016 till \n31.12.2017. A statement indicating the State/UT -wise quantum of seizures \nis enclosed as Annexure.  \nThe Ministry of Home Affairs, Ministry of Finance, Reserve Bank of India, \nSecurity and Intelligence Agencies of the Centre and States are working in \ncoordination to prevent the illegal activities related to FICN.  \n(c): Information received from security and intelligence agencies \nindicates that Pakistan has been involved in manufacturing and smuggling \nof FICN into India. However, as per the available information, no instance \nof seizure of Pakistan printed High Quality Fak e Indian Currency Notes has \ncome to notice post demonetization. \n***** \n\n \n \n \nANNEXURE \nL.S.US.Q.NO 643 FOR 06.02.2018 \n \nNATIONAL CRIME RECORDS BUREAU (MHA) \nState/UT-wise and Denomination-wise Statement of Counterfeit Currency (Reported as Seized by SCRBx) \n \nPeriodical Report from : 09/11/2016 to : 31/12/2017* (after Demonitisation) \n \nAnnexed with Reply to Lok Sabha Unst